From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: no magnification or colour transforms the device cannot compose

Magnification, colour inversion and colour correction are applied by
SurfaceFlinger as a scale or a colour matrix on the composed display. PW3's
composer works on the CPU and does neither; SurfaceFlinger then composes
every frame with GLES, which is CPU-emulated here (SwiftShader). Measured on
Test V40.1: magnification shows correctly but entering or leaving it costs
SurfaceFlinger more than 4 s of CPU, and every frame while magnified is as
slow; with colour inversion SurfaceFlinger stayed at full load. Colour
correction has nothing to correct on a grey-level panel. The product says so
(ro.pw3.disable_display_transforms=true) and Accessibility shows none of the
three, nor does search; the system's font size and display size remain.

Search also no longer offers the entries 0003 and AOSP leave off this page on
a device without them (power button ends call, lock screen rotation, large
pointer, click after the pointer stops, mono audio, text-to-speech output,
the accessibility shortcut): found by search, they led to a page without
them.

